=== OLS vs lasso CO_Mega model, ribonn TE, muscle ===

[1] Coefficients
  lasso alpha (10-fold CV, standardized predictors) = 0.00335
  lasso keeps 52 of 61 codons; sets 9 to exactly 0: TTT, TCG, CAG, CGT, ATC, GTC, GTG, GAA, GGC
  of those 9, 9 are nominally significant (p < 0.05) in the OLS model; OLS has 58 nominally significant codons overall, 49 of them kept by the lasso
  OLS vs lasso coefficients: Pearson r = 0.9937, Spearman rho = 0.9949; slope of lasso on OLS among kept codons = 0.922 (shrinkage)
  coefficient mean / SD across the 61 codons: OLS -54.967 / 4.196, lasso -0.509 / 3.882
  NOTE: the 61 sense-codon frequencies of a gene sum to ~1 (see [2]), so together with the intercept the OLS
  coefficients are only identified up to a common shift (add c to every coefficient, subtract c from the
  intercept): the huge OLS intercept / mean coefficient are that arbitrary shift, not an effect. Only the
  differences between codons (SD, correlations, slope above, all shift-invariant) are meaningful; the lasso
  penalty picks the sparse solution, which is why its intercept and mean coefficient stay small.
  intercept: OLS 54.8600, lasso 0.4174

